API.md §5.7: an importer b that writes no output leaves the fix; with every package loaded Item.dwLevel is renamed.
-- project.canon --
project acme {
  canon: "0.1"
}
-- apply --
-- a/a.canon --
package a

/// Item.
record Item {
  /// Level.
  dwLevel: Int
}
-- b/b.canon --
package b

import a

let x: a.Item = { dwLevel: 1 }
-- findings.txt --
warning[W0001]  a/a.canon:6:3
  field dwLevel keeps the legacy prefix dw in its Canon name: rename it level (canon rename keeps the old wire name with @json where a load or a data emit reads the field)

0 errors, 1 warning in 2 packages (…)
fix W0001 a/a.canon:6:3 {"ops":[{"op":"renameName","path":"a:Item.dwLevel","name":"level"}]}
after the first fix:
0 errors, 0 warnings in 2 packages (…)
